IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ia-fip`

-- Iowa family investment program -- the seat of the applicant (the parent or other specified relative applying for, or
-- receiving, FIP cash assistance for a child).
--
-- "Is my grandchild a 'child'? Can I apply? Are our savings under the limit? Does our income pass? How much would we get
-- each month? When must the department decide? I got a JOBS reminder letter: by when must I answer?" Every answer is
-- built from the rules in ia-fip.l4.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Iowa family investment program -- my questions`

§§ `Who can get FIP`

@export Is this young person a "child" for Iowa's family investment program (Iowa Code 239B.1(3))?
GIVEN `their age` IS A NUMBER @desc The young person's age in whole years
      `they are married` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the young person is married
      `they are 18 and finishing high school full-time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If they are 18: whether they are full-time in high school or an equivalency program and expected to finish before turning 19
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this young person a child for FIP` IF
    `is a child` `their age` `they are married` `they are 18 and finishing high school full-time`

@export Am I a relative who can apply for FIP for this child (a "specified relative", Iowa Code 239B.1(13), 239B.2(1))?
GIVEN `my relationship to the child` IS A `Relationship to the child` @desc How you are related to the child, by blood, marriage or adoption, now or at any time (or as the spouse of such a relative)
      `the child lives or will live with me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the child lives with you, or will live with you
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I apply for this child` IF
        `is a specified relative` `my relationship to the child`
    AND `the child lives or will live with me`

§§ `Resources and income`

@export Are our family's resources within the FIP limit (Iowa Code 239B.7(6) to (8))?
GIVEN `we already receive FIP` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your family already receives FIP (a participant family, limit $5,000) rather than applying (limit $2,000)
      `our cash, bank accounts and other resources` IS A NUMBER @desc The total of your family's cash, bank and other countable resources, not counting one motor vehicle, an individual development account, or tools of the trade
      `our equity in any vehicles beyond the first` IS A NUMBER @desc The equity value of any motor vehicles other than one
      `the value of self-employment tools and capital assets` IS A NUMBER @desc The value of the tools of the trade or capital assets of a self-employed family member ($10,000 of it is disregarded)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are our resources within the FIP limit` IF
    `is within the resource limitation` `we already receive FIP`
        (`countable resources` `our cash, bank accounts and other resources` `our equity in any vehicles beyond the first` `the value of self-employment tools and capital assets`)

@export Does our family's monthly income pass the FIP income tests (IAC 441-41.27, 41.28)?
GIVEN `the number of people in our eligible group` IS A NUMBER @desc The children and the parents (or the relative whose needs are included) living together, not counting anyone receiving SSI, an unborn child, or a member absent more than three months in jail or prison
      `we already receive FIP` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your family already receives FIP (the standard of need test applies only on application)
      `our monthly earned income` IS A NUMBER @desc The group's total gross monthly earnings: wages, tips, commissions, and net profit from self-employment
      `our monthly unearned income` IS A NUMBER @desc The group's other monthly income counted by FIP, after withheld taxes: unemployment, social security, support received directly, and so on
      `support we pay for children outside the home` IS A NUMBER @desc Court-ordered support actually paid each month for children not living with you, and other income diversions allowed by the rules (0 if none)
      `our allowable special needs` IS A NUMBER @desc Any special needs the department allows each month under IAC 441-41.28(3) (0 if none)
GIVETH AN `Income test result`
`Does our income pass the FIP tests` MEANS
    `the income tests` `the number of people in our eligible group` `our allowable special needs`
        (`Monthly income` WITH
            `gross nonexempt earned income` IS `our monthly earned income`
            `nonexempt unearned income` IS `our monthly unearned income`
            `income diversions` IS `support we pay for children outside the home`)
        `we already receive FIP`

§§ `How much we would get`

DECLARE `My FIP result` IS ONE OF
    `a monthly cash grant` HAS `dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `no grant: there is no child, or no parent or specified relative, in the family (239B.1(6))`
    `no grant: the application is not made by a specified relative the child lives with (239B.2(1))`
    `no grant: the family's resources are over the limit (239B.7(7))`
    `no grant: the family's income fails a test` HAS `the test` IS AN `Income test result`
    `no grant: another condition of 239B.2 is not met (the written statement, information, or child support cooperation)`

@export How much FIP cash assistance would my family get each month (Iowa Code 239B.2, 239B.3, 239B.7; IAC 441-41.27, 41.28)?
GIVEN `the number of children` IS A NUMBER @desc How many children (under 18, or 18 and finishing high school) are in the family
      `my relationship to the child` IS A `Relationship to the child` @desc How you, the person applying, are related to the child
      `the child lives or will live with me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the child lives, or will live, with you
      `the number of people in our eligible group` IS A NUMBER @desc The children and the parents (or the relative whose needs are included) living together, not counting anyone receiving SSI, an unborn child, or a member absent more than three months in jail or prison
      `we already receive FIP` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your family already receives FIP
      `our cash, bank accounts and other resources` IS A NUMBER @desc The total of your family's cash, bank and other countable resources, not counting one motor vehicle, an individual development account, or tools of the trade
      `our equity in any vehicles beyond the first` IS A NUMBER @desc The equity value of any motor vehicles other than one
      `the value of self-employment tools and capital assets` IS A NUMBER @desc The value of a self-employed family member's tools of the trade or capital assets
      `our monthly earned income` IS A NUMBER @desc The group's total gross monthly earnings
      `our monthly unearned income` IS A NUMBER @desc The group's other monthly income counted by FIP, after withheld taxes
      `support we pay for children outside the home` IS A NUMBER @desc Court-ordered support actually paid each month for children not living with you, and other diversions allowed by the rules (0 if none)
      `our allowable special needs` IS A NUMBER @desc Any special needs the department allows each month (0 if none)
      `we sign the written statement or family investment agreement, or are exempt` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your family commits to the written statement of first steps (or the family investment agreement), or is exempt
      `we provide the information the department asks for` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you provide the information the department requests
      `I cooperate with child support services, or the department found good cause` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you cooperate with child support services where a parent is absent, or the department has found good cause or another exception (answer yes if no parent is absent)
GIVETH A `My FIP result`
`How much FIP would we get` MEANS
    IF NOT (`is a family` `the number of children` (`is a specified relative` `my relationship to the child`))
    THEN `no grant: there is no child, or no parent or specified relative, in the family (239B.1(6))`
    ELSE IF NOT (`Can I apply for this child` `my relationship to the child` `the child lives or will live with me`)
         THEN `no grant: the application is not made by a specified relative the child lives with (239B.2(1))`
         ELSE IF NOT resourcesOk
              THEN `no grant: the family's resources are over the limit (239B.7(7))`
              ELSE CONSIDER incomeTest
                   WHEN `meets the income tests` THEN
                       IF `meets the 239B.2 conditions` conditions
                       THEN `a monthly cash grant` (`the FIP grant` `the number of people in our eligible group` `our allowable special needs` income)
                       ELSE `no grant: another condition of 239B.2 is not met (the written statement, information, or child support cooperation)`
                   OTHERWISE `no grant: the family's income fails a test` incomeTest
    WHERE
        income MEANS `Monthly income` WITH
            `gross nonexempt earned income` IS `our monthly earned income`
            `nonexempt unearned income` IS `our monthly unearned income`
            `income diversions` IS `support we pay for children outside the home`
        resourcesOk MEANS `is within the resource limitation` `we already receive FIP` (`countable resources` `our cash, bank accounts and other resources` `our equity in any vehicles beyond the first` `the value of self-employment tools and capital assets`)
        incomeTest MEANS `the income tests` `the number of people in our eligible group` `our allowable special needs` income `we already receive FIP`
        conditions MEANS `Conditions` WITH
            `the application is made by the specified relative with whom the child resides or will reside` IS TRUE
            `the family meets the income guidelines` IS TRUE
            `the family meets the resource guidelines` IS TRUE
            `the family commits to the written statement or is exempt` IS `we sign the written statement or family investment agreement, or are exempt`
            `the family provides the requested information` IS `we provide the information the department asks for`
            `cooperation with child support is given, or the department finds good cause or another exception` IS `I cooperate with child support services, or the department found good cause`

@export What are the FIP payment standard and standard of need for a group of our size (IAC 441-41.28(2))? Returns the monthly payment standard.
GIVEN `the number of people in our eligible group` IS A NUMBER @desc How many people are in your eligible group
      `our allowable special needs` IS A NUMBER @desc Any special needs the department allows each month (0 if none)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is our FIP payment standard` MEANS `payment standard` `the number of people in our eligible group` `our allowable special needs`

§§ `Deadlines`

@export By what date must the department authorize notice of its decision on my FIP application (Iowa Code 239B.3(1)(b))?
GIVEN `the day I applied` IS A DATE @desc The date of your application
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must the department decide` MEANS `the day I applied` PLUS 30

-- Only for a participant who missed, or did not make, a JOBS orientation appointment and was sent a reminder letter.
@export I was sent a reminder letter about my PROMISE JOBS orientation: by what date must I respond, so that I am not treated as choosing a limited benefit plan (Iowa Code 239B.9(3)(a))?
GIVEN `the day the reminder letter was mailed` IS A DATE @desc The mailing date of the reminder letter
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I answer the reminder letter` MEANS `the day the reminder letter was mailed` PLUS 10

-- Only for a participant in a limited benefit plan.
@export May I now reconsider my limited benefit plan (Iowa Code 239B.9(4))?
GIVEN `this is my first limited benefit plan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether this is the first limited benefit plan you have chosen
      `the plan's effective date` IS A DATE @desc The effective date of the limited benefit plan, from the department's notice
      `the period of ineligibility in days` IS A NUMBER @desc For a subsequent plan: the period of ineligibility the notice specifies, in days (six months or less)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I reconsider my limited benefit plan` IF
    `may reconsider the limited benefit plan` `this is my first limited benefit plan` (`today` MINUS `the plan's effective date`) `the period of ineligibility in days`

§§ `Child support and funeral expenses`

@export Must I cooperate with child support services as a condition of FIP (Iowa Code 239B.2(6))?
GIVEN `a parent of the child is absent from the home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a parent of the child lives outside the home
      `the department found good cause or another exception` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the department has found good cause or another exception for you, for example under a family investment agreement safety plan for family or domestic violence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I cooperate with child support` IF
        `a parent of the child is absent from the home`
    AND (NOT `the department found good cause or another exception`)

-- Only on the death of a child in the program.
@export What is the most the department may pay toward the funeral of a child who was in FIP (Iowa Code 239B.3(4))?
GIVEN `the estate can pay the funeral` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the child left an estate that can be probated with enough to pay the funeral expenses
      `death payments due from insurance, social security or veterans' benefits` IS A NUMBER @desc Payments due to the child's estate or beneficiary from life insurance, a death or funeral benefit, social security, railroad retirement or veterans' benefits
GIVETH A NUMBER
`The most toward the funeral` MEANS
    `the most the department may pay toward funeral expenses` `the estate can pay the funeral` `death payments due from insurance, social security or veterans' benefits`
